    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix has been successfully applied and compiled. The change I made extracts all arguments directly from `process.argv` starting from the 'gate' keyword, ensuring that flags like `--ci` are properly passed through to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Summary of the fix:**\n\n**Problem:** When running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed to the frai-gate CLI because commander.js's variadic argument handling doesn't properly capture options for pass-through commands.\n\n**Solution:** Instead of relying on commander's `args` parameter, the gate command now extracts arguments directly from `process.argv` using:\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.findIndex((arg) => arg === 'gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n```\n\nThis ensures all arguments (including `--ci`) are properly forwarded to the spawned frai-gate process, which will then create the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` workflow file.\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready to use. The workflow file will now be created when running `frai gate init --ci`.",
